UPDATE v57.forge_nodes
SET outputs = '[{"key":"core_loop","label":"Core Loop","type":"connection","format":"core_loop","prompt":"Emit the named loop (4 steps: action / response / feedback / reward), duration under 15 min, retention hook, win/lose with fail-state consequences.","uses":{"inputs":["design_pillars","feel_statement"],"siblings_if_present":[]}},{"key":"mechanic_specs","label":"Mechanic Specs","type":"connection","format":"list<mechanic_spec>","prompt":"Emit all mechanics, each with concrete rules and real numbers, plus an integration map of how they affect each other. INSTANCING TRIGGER: fans out one prototype lane per mechanic at the Prototype Specification node.","uses":{"inputs":["design_pillars"],"siblings_if_present":["core_loop"]},"note":"ENGINEERING-READY (TDD §B). Each mechanic_spec carries: quantified rules, io, dependencies, state_machine, components, public_api, edge_cases, >=1 testable acceptance_criterion, graph_edges, slice_scope. Still the fan-out trigger for the Prototype Specification node."},{"key":"feel_statement","label":"Feel Statement","type":"connection","format":"feel_statement","prompt":"Re-emit the feel statement grounded in the mechanics (level=mechanics); show how the mechanics express the pillar feel. Replaces the upstream value for all downstream nodes. ↻ consumed-and-refined.","uses":{"inputs":["feel_statement"],"siblings_if_present":["mechanic_specs","core_loop"]}},{"key":"mechanics_engineering","label":"Mechanics Engineering","type":"connection","format":"list<mechanic_engineering>","prompt":"SOURCE OF TRUTH — the mechanic list is FIXED by the sibling mechanic_specs: its Master Mechanics Table is the authoritative roster. Emit EXACTLY one record per row of that table, 1:1, preserving its quantified numbers verbatim. Do NOT invent, drop, merge, split or re-derive mechanics; the ONLY permitted name change is PascalCase-ising the table''s name (\"Scene Reading\" → SceneReading). Every row must appear here, and nothing else may. INCOMPLETE SOURCE: if a row has no detailed spec section in mechanic_specs, still emit its record from the table row and mark each unbacked field [PENDING owner=3.2 resolve-by=Balance-Pass] — never invent the missing detail, and never silently omit the mechanic. CONFLICTS: if a rule contradicts the 3.0 input_map_skeleton, KEEP the mechanic_specs number and flag it [CONFLICT owner=3.0 resolve-by=TDD assembly] — never silently rewrite it. Then, for each: one engineering-ready record (TDD §B shape): name (PascalCase), type {feature|system|mechanic}, status/version (semver), sliceScope (bool), player_facing {goal, loop, ui_feedback (UI_* ids), tuning_levers[]}, rules[] (QUANTIFIED — concrete numbers), limits, authority, determinism, io {player_inputs[] (action names from 3.0 input_map_skeleton), system_inputs[], outputs[] (events+payload)}, persistence (none | {what,format,trigger}), dependencies[] {kind,id PascalCase — every id must resolve}, preconditions[], state_machine {states,initial,transitions} or explicit N/A, components[] (config/runtime separated), public_api, edge_cases[], acceptance_criteria[] (testable, each tagged EditMode|PlayMode, >=1), narrative_ref?, graph_edges[], companion_spec_yaml (the §C block with validationGates). Document-level: support_systems[] {id PascalCase, purpose, public_surface, spec} for every non-mechanic dependency id (→ §B-S).","uses":{"siblings_if_present":["mechanic_specs","core_loop"]},"note":"NEW in v2.7.0 — engineering-grade output for the TDD (3.12). DERIVED FROM mechanic_specs (1:1, declared in uses.siblings_if_present), which remains UNTOUCHED because the GDD (3.8 §3) consumes it. R1 mitigation: two outputs, one node, zero GDD regression — but the two MUST stay reconciled. v2.7.1: was PARALLEL and unbound, which let it re-derive its own mechanic set (10 → 6, names renamed, PowerNode invented) and split the GDD and TDD into two different games."},{"key":"core_gameplay_spec","label":"Core Gameplay Spec","type":"asset","format":"docx","prompt":"Write the core gameplay spec: loop, mechanics with real numbers, difficulty curve with escalation points, integration map. Identical to the connections.","uses":{"inputs":["design_pillars","feel_statement"],"siblings_if_present":["core_loop","mechanic_specs"]}}]'::jsonb,
    updated_at = now()
WHERE node_key = '3.2' AND phase = 'pre-production';
